## Recon findings (verified at HEAD)
- Desktop shell: `desktop/src/App.tsx` has `const modes: readonly ModeRegistration[]` currently registering only `clean` (`<CleanWorkbench bridge={bridge} coordinator={coordinator} locale={presentation.locale} />`). `desktop/src/app-shell/AppShell.tsx` `MODE_IDS = ["clean","software","optimize","analyze","status"]` with hash routing `#/analyze` already supported. Register the new AnalyzePage the same way CleanWorkbench is registered.
- Desktop clean mode template: `desktop/src/modes/clean/{CleanWorkbench.tsx,reducer.ts,reducer.test.ts,index.ts}` — follow its structure/conventions for `desktop/src/modes/analyze/`.
- TUI: `crates/devsweep-cli/src/tui/shell/mod.rs` freezes `ModeId::Analyze` but `TuiShell` registers only `ModeRegistration::clean()`. `crates/devsweep-cli/src/tui/modes/clean/mod.rs` is the existing mode template. TUI app state/reducer/job machinery: `crates/devsweep-cli/src/tui/app/{mod.rs,jobs.rs,worker.rs,events.rs,input.rs}` (has `cancel_active_job`, `JobKind`, job lifecycle effects). TUI i18n via `crate::i18n::catalogue(locale)` reading the resources catalogue. You will need to register the analyze mode in the shell (add a `ModeRegistration::analyze()` constructor following the clean pattern) and wire an analyze mode state/reducer into the TUI app — mode registration and reducer wiring are in scope; the shell's frozen `ModeId` set, the CLI parser, and the frozen snapshot DTO schema are NOT to be edited.
- How the TUI obtains a snapshot: it must run the core read-only analyze through its existing job/worker pattern with cooperative cancellation (core exposes `analyze_path(root, cancel_observer, progress_sink)`; see `crates/devsweep-cli/src/application/commands/analyze.rs` and `crates/devsweep-core/src/analysis/mod.rs` for the exact API and the cancel observer trait). The presentation layer itself performs no filesystem access — selectors/layout operate purely on the snapshot DTO. Leaving the Analyze mode (shell navigation change) must cancel and join the running analyze job before releasing view state (R4). Stale operation-id/sequence IPC events must be rejected (desktop side, matching `desktop/src-tauri/src/analyze.rs` event contracts).
