## What to build (summary; implement.md/prd/design are authoritative)
1. Pure bounded views: immutable current-directory selectors (by node id), deterministic 200-row paging, breadcrumbs, search/sort, focus anchors; pure squarified treemap layout returning at most 512 known-size child tiles + 1 aggregated `Other` tile (exact remaining known bytes/count recorded; unknown/partial descendants never receive invented area; deterministic rounding; zero/equal/extreme/tiny sizes handled). TUI: proportional lower-bound bars + same breadcrumbs, viewport-only rendering.
2. State/IPC/a11y wiring: mode-local reducers consuming generated DTOs, stale event rejection, linked treemap↔paged list, keyboard drill-down/up, logical focus order, labelled rectangles (accessible list is the canonical complete route), reduced motion, contrast, bilingual states (empty/loading/canceling/partial/error/complete, available/partial/unknown/permission/unsupported), resize, long paths. No select/delete/cleanup affordance anywhere. Cancel/join through the shell on navigation/close.
3. Gates: `cargo test -p devsweep-cli tui::modes::analyze` (use plain `cargo`; the `rtk` wrapper may not exist — if a command in implement.md starts with `rtk`, drop the prefix), `just desktop-web-check`, `just desktop-build`, `git diff --check`, and finally `just ci`. Render-budget gate on the 250k fixture: ≤513 rectangles, ≤900 rendered DOM elements, p95 pure layout ≤50 ms, p95 React commit ≤100 ms, nearest-rank p95 (sort ascending, pick ceil(0.95*n)-th; for 30 samples = 29th), five warm-ups then 30 measured navigations; record host/build/webview versions, raw durations, and DOM/memory counts in the evidence JSON. A budget miss is a STOP and report — never raise a cap.

